Carafe: the front end queue holds 4 MB instead of 1 MB, so a heavy frame of effect calls no longer waits for room.
With the profiler on, every buffer or texture lock that has to wait for the queue to run out is counted by its pool,
usage, lock flags, and whether the buffer was bound for drawing or the texture is a render target, and logged next to
the drains by caller as one "locks that wait" line every 600 presents.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

